Task 1: Configure SSL for Satellite
Subtask 1.1: Verify Current Satellite Installation
First, let's check the current status of your Satellite installation and identify the SSL configuration.

Check Satellite status:
satellite-maintain service status
Verify current SSL configuration:
satellite-installer --help | grep -i ssl
Check current certificate information:
openssl x509 -in /etc/pki/katello/certs/katello-apache.crt -text -noout
Subtask 1.2: Generate SSL Certificate Signing Request (CSR)
Now we'll create a proper SSL certificate for our Satellite server.

Create a directory for SSL operations:
mkdir -p /root/satellite-ssl
cd /root/satellite-ssl
Generate a private key:
openssl genrsa -out satellite.key 2048
chmod 600 satellite.key
Create a certificate signing request configuration file:
cat > satellite.conf << EOF
[req]
distinguished_name = req_distinguished_name
req_extensions = v3_req
prompt = no

[req_distinguished_name]
C = US
ST = YourState
L = YourCity
O = YourOrganization
OU = IT Department
CN = $(hostname -f)

[v3_req]
keyUsage = keyEncipherment, dataEncipherment
extendedKeyUsage = serverAuth
subjectAltName = @alt_names

[alt_names]
DNS.1 = $(hostname -f)
DNS.2 = $(hostname -s)
IP.1 = $(ip route get 1 | awk '{print $7}' | head -1)
EOF
Generate the certificate signing request:
openssl req -new -key satellite.key -out satellite.csr -config satellite.conf
Subtask 1.3: Create Self-Signed Certificate for Lab Environment
For this lab, we'll create a self-signed certificate. In production, you would send the CSR to a trusted Certificate Authority.

Generate self-signed certificate:
openssl x509 -req -in satellite.csr -signkey satellite.key -out satellite.crt -days 365 -extensions v3_req -extfile satellite.conf
Verify the certificate:
openssl x509 -in satellite.crt -text -noout | head -20
Create certificate bundle:
cp satellite.crt satellite-bundle.crt
Task 2: Set up Internal Certificate Management for Satellite
Subtask 2.1: Configure Satellite with Custom SSL Certificate
Now we'll configure Satellite to use our custom SSL certificate.

Stop Satellite services:
satellite-maintain service stop
Backup existing certificates:
mkdir -p /root/satellite-ssl-backup
cp -r /etc/pki/katello/ /root/satellite-ssl-backup/
Run satellite-installer with custom certificates:
satellite-installer \
  --certs-server-cert /root/satellite-ssl/satellite.crt \
  --certs-server-key /root/satellite-ssl/satellite.key \
  --certs-server-ca-cert /root/satellite-ssl/satellite-bundle.crt \
  --certs-update-server-ca true
Subtask 2.2: Configure Internal Certificate Authority
Let's set up an internal CA for managing client certificates and other internal SSL needs.

Create CA directory structure:
mkdir -p /etc/satellite-ca/{certs,crl,newcerts,private}
chmod 700 /etc/satellite-ca/private
touch /etc/satellite-ca/index.txt
echo 1000 > /etc/satellite-ca/serial
Create CA configuration file:
cat > /etc/satellite-ca/openssl.cnf << EOF
[ ca ]
default_ca = CA_default

[ CA_default ]
dir               = /etc/satellite-ca
certs             = \$dir/certs
crl_dir           = \$dir/crl
new_certs_dir     = \$dir/newcerts
database          = \$dir/index.txt
serial            = \$dir/serial
RANDFILE          = \$dir/private/.rand

private_key       = \$dir/private/ca.key
certificate       = \$dir/certs/ca.crt

crlnumber         = \$dir/crlnumber
crl               = \$dir/crl/ca.crl
crl_extensions    = crl_ext
default_crl_days  = 30

default_md        = sha256
name_opt          = ca_default
cert_opt          = ca_default
default_days      = 375
preserve          = no
policy            = policy_strict

[ policy_strict ]
countryName             = match
stateOrProvinceName     = match
organizationName        = match
organizationalUnitName  = optional
commonName              = supplied
emailAddress            = optional

[ req ]
default_bits        = 2048
distinguished_name  = req_distinguished_name
string_mask         = utf8only
default_md          = sha256
x509_extensions     = v3_ca

[ req_distinguished_name ]
countryName                     = Country Name (2 letter code)
stateOrProvinceName             = State or Province Name
localityName                    = Locality Name
0.organizationName              = Organization Name
organizationalUnitName          = Organizational Unit Name
commonName                      = Common Name
emailAddress                    = Email Address

[ v3_ca ]
subjectKeyIdentifier = hash
authorityKeyIdentifier = keyid:always,issuer
basicConstraints = critical, CA:true
keyUsage = critical, digitalSignature, cRLSign, keyCertSign

[ server_cert ]
basicConstraints = CA:FALSE
nsCertType = server
nsComment = "OpenSSL Generated Server Certificate"
subjectKeyIdentifier = hash
authorityKeyIdentifier = keyid,issuer:always
keyUsage = critical, digitalSignature, keyEncipherment
extendedKeyUsage = serverAuth
EOF
Generate CA private key:
openssl genrsa -out /etc/satellite-ca/private/ca.key 4096
chmod 400 /etc/satellite-ca/private/ca.key
Create CA certificate:
openssl req -config /etc/satellite-ca/openssl.cnf \
  -key /etc/satellite-ca/private/ca.key \
  -new -x509 -days 7300 -sha256 -extensions v3_ca \
  -out /etc/satellite-ca/certs/ca.crt \
  -subj "/C=US/ST=YourState/L=YourCity/O=YourOrganization/OU=IT Department/CN=Satellite Internal CA"
Subtask 2.3: Configure Satellite Services for SSL
Update Satellite configuration for SSL:
satellite-installer \
  --foreman-ssl true \
  --certs-update-server-ca true
Configure Apache SSL settings:
cat >> /etc/httpd/conf.d/05-foreman-ssl.conf << EOF

# Additional SSL Security Headers
Header always set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
Header always set X-Content-Type-Options nosniff
Header always set X-Frame-Options DENY
Header always set X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block"
EOF
Restart Satellite services:
satellite-maintain service restart
Task 3: Ensure All Communication with Satellite is Encrypted and Secure
Subtask 3.1: Configure Secure Communication Protocols
Update SSL/TLS protocols in Apache:
sed -i 's/SSLProtocol all -SSLv2 -SSLv3/SSLProtocol all -SSLv2 -SSLv3 -TLSv1 -TLSv1.1/' /etc/httpd/conf.d/ssl.conf
Configure strong cipher suites:
cat >> /etc/httpd/conf.d/ssl.conf << EOF

# Strong SSL Configuration
SSLCipherSuite ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384:ECDHE-RSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384
SSLHonorCipherOrder on
SSLCompression off
SSLUseStapling on
SSLStaplingCache shmcb:/var/run/ocsp(128000)
EOF
Subtask 3.2: Configure Database SSL Connections
Configure PostgreSQL for SSL:
# Enable SSL in PostgreSQL
sed -i "s/#ssl = off/ssl = on/" /var/lib/pgsql/data/postgresql.conf

# Configure SSL certificates for PostgreSQL
cp /root/satellite-ssl/satellite.crt /var/lib/pgsql/data/server.crt
cp /root/satellite-ssl/satellite.key /var/lib/pgsql/data/server.key
chown postgres:postgres /var/lib/pgsql/data/server.*
chmod 600 /var/lib/pgsql/data/server.key
Update PostgreSQL client authentication:
echo "hostssl all all 127.0.0.1/32 md5" >> /var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf
Restart PostgreSQL:
systemctl restart postgresql
Subtask 3.3: Configure Pulp for SSL
Update Pulp configuration for SSL:
cat > /etc/pulp/settings.py << EOF
CONTENT_ORIGIN = "https://$(hostname -f)"
ALLOWED_HOSTS = ["$(hostname -f)", "$(hostname -s)", "localhost"]
DATABASES = {
    'default': {
        'ENGINE': 'django.db.backends.postgresql_psycopg2',
        'NAME': 'pulpcore',
        'USER': 'pulp',
        'PASSWORD': 'pulp',
        'HOST': 'localhost',
        'PORT': '',
        'OPTIONS': {'sslmode': 'require'},
    }
}
EOF
Restart Pulp services:
systemctl restart pulpcore-api pulpcore-content pulpcore-worker@*
Subtask 3.4: Verify SSL Configuration
Test SSL certificate:
openssl s_client -connect $(hostname -f):443 -servername $(hostname -f) < /dev/null
Check SSL configuration with SSL Labs-like test:
curl -I https://$(hostname -f)/
Verify all services are using SSL:
netstat -tlnp | grep :443
ss -tlnp | grep :443
Test Satellite web interface:
curl -k -I https://$(hostname -f)/users/login
Subtask 3.5: Configure Client Certificate Authentication (Optional)
Generate client certificate:
cd /root/satellite-ssl

# Generate client private key
openssl genrsa -out client.key 2048

# Generate client certificate request
openssl req -new -key client.key -out client.csr \
  -subj "/C=US/ST=YourState/L=YourCity/O=YourOrganization/OU=IT Department/CN=satellite-client"

# Sign client certificate with our CA
openssl ca -config /etc/satellite-ca/openssl.cnf \
  -extensions server_cert -days 365 -notext -md sha256 \
  -in client.csr -out client.crt -batch
Configure Apache for client certificate authentication:
cat >> /etc/httpd/conf.d/05-foreman-ssl.conf << EOF

# Client Certificate Authentication (Optional)
<Location "/api">
    SSLVerifyClient optional
    SSLVerifyDepth 2
    SSLCACertificateFile /etc/satellite-ca/certs/ca.crt
</Location>
EOF
Verification and Testing
Test SSL Configuration
Comprehensive SSL test:
#!/bin/bash
echo "=== SSL Configuration Test ==="
echo "1. Testing HTTPS connectivity..."
curl -k -s -o /dev/null -w "HTTP Status: %{http_code}\n" https://$(hostname -f)/

echo "2. Testing SSL certificate..."
echo | openssl s_client -connect $(hostname -f):443 2>/dev/null | openssl x509 -noout -dates

echo "3. Testing SSL protocols..."
for protocol in tls1_2 tls1_3; do
    echo -n "Testing $protocol: "
    echo | openssl s_client -connect $(hostname -f):443 -$protocol 2>/dev/null | grep -q "Verify return code: 0" && echo "OK" || echo "FAILED"
done

echo "4. Testing cipher suites..."
nmap --script ssl-enum-ciphers -p 443 $(hostname -f) | grep -A 10 "TLSv1.2"
Save and run the test script:
chmod +x /root/ssl-test.sh
/root/ssl-test.sh
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Certificate Verification Failed
Problem: SSL certificate verification fails Solution:

# Check certificate chain
openssl verify -CAfile /etc/satellite-ca/certs/ca.crt /root/satellite-ssl/satellite.crt

# Verify certificate matches private key
openssl x509 -noout -modulus -in /root/satellite-ssl/satellite.crt | openssl md5
openssl rsa -noout -modulus -in /root/satellite-ssl/satellite.key | openssl md5
Issue 2: Services Not Starting After SSL Configuration
Problem: Satellite services fail to start after SSL configuration Solution:

# Check service logs
journalctl -u httpd -f
journalctl -u foreman -f

# Verify file permissions
ls -la /root/satellite-ssl/
chown root:root /root/satellite-ssl/*
chmod 644 /root/satellite-ssl/*.crt
chmod 600 /root/satellite-ssl/*.key
Issue 3: Browser Certificate Warnings
Problem: Browser shows certificate warnings Solution:

# Add CA certificate to system trust store
cp /etc/satellite-ca/certs/ca.crt /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/satellite-ca.crt
update-ca-trust
