Why This Matters: SSL/TLS encryption is critical for protecting sensitive data in enterprise environments. Satellite servers often manage thousands of systems and contain sensitive configuration data, user credentials, and system information. By implementing proper SSL security:

Data Protection: All communication between clients and Satellite is encrypted, preventing eavesdropping and man-in-the-middle attacks
Authentication: SSL certificates provide server authentication, ensuring clients connect to legitimate Satellite servers
Compliance: Many regulatory frameworks require encryption of sensitive data in transit
Trust: Internal Certificate Authorities provide centralized trust management for your organization's infrastructure
This knowledge is essential for the Red Hat Certified Specialist in Deployment and Systems Management exam and real-world enterprise deployments where security is paramount.
